sheetCart[0] | 6, 6, 32, 32 | The first frame of the boat in a fishery at its first level (and every other level after that), used when travelling north. Turned a quarter, half and three quarters clockwise, it serves east, south and west. A boat being rowed switches frames four times a second and stays on the first frame while fishing; a boat moored in the fishery keeps one of the two frames, picked at random.
